 "notes": "West side of the Col de Marie-Blanque from Escot (Aspe valley), as in the app (start 330 m, 9.2 km, summit 1035 m). km 0 = the junction in Escot village where the D294 Route du Barescou leaves Rue de Labuchoa (~334 m DEM), 0.66 km after the N134; starting at the N134 junction itself would give 9.8 km, so the app profile (9.2 km) starts in the village (DEM per-km fit rms ~1.3 %). Route: D294 only — up the narrow Barescou valley (gentle 3-6 %), several bridges over the Barescou, into the forest at ~km 4.5, then a nearly straight 10-13 % ramp with a single hairpin ~330 m below the col. Coordinates are on the Overture/OSM road geometry; km are routed distances from the foot (routed 9.16 km vs 9.2 km). The app landmark 'stone bridge at the Barescou' (km 2.3) has no bridge in the map data there; the bridges in the data are at km 1.1, 3.9 and 4.5.",
